      "Title: Postmill: Troubleshooting navigation and reply targeting\nDescription: Key signals and pitfalls when navigating to threads and targeting specific replies.\n- A 404 Not Found page indicates the current URL does not lead to a valid post; navigate to the home page to restart.\n- Use the 'Forums' link to access the list of available forums if the post is not visible on the home page.\n- Ensure you are on the thread's comment page (URL contains '/comments' or similar) before attempting to reply.\n- The 'Reply' link must be clicked specifically under the target comment to open the correct reply form.\n- The reply textbox is often labeled 'Comment' and may be required; ensure the text is filled before posting.\n- If the page shows a list of posts rather than comments, click the 'comments' link to enter the thread.\n- Verify the reply appears on the thread after clicking 'Post' to confirm success."
